From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v4lkyr <valkyr23@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:15:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: zero UVM channel notifier arrays after allocation

channelAllocate() and nvGpuOpsPagingChannelAllocate() hand the
per-channel notifier array (error, work submit token, key rotation) to
UVM without clearing it. The backing sysmem is only zeroed when
NVreg_InitializeSystemMemoryAllocations is set (the default); with it
set to 0 the pages can still hold data from a previous user.

UVM treats any non-zero error notifier status as an RC error.
channel_init() reads it while starting the channel's first push, so a
stale value latches a UVM global fatal error, RM reports Xid 154 with
the OS reboot recovery action, and CUDA is unusable until reboot. The
work submit token is also read from the notifier page before every
doorbell write, and the key rotation status is compared against
UVM_KEY_ROTATION_STATUS_PENDING. All three expect 0 at start.

Clear the whole array once it is mapped, before the channel is
allocated and the notifier published, in both paths.

Upstream PR 1539 (v4lkyr), tested by the author on 620.70.06 with 200
cuInit/cuCtxCreate/cuMemAllocManaged/cuCtxDestroy cycles. Comment
reworded to name the module parameter that makes the pages non-zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/nv_gpu_ops.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/nv_gpu_ops.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/nv_gpu_ops.c
index 55c1bd31..c821dc66 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/nv_gpu_ops.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/nv_gpu_ops.c
@@ -6123,6 +6123,16 @@ static NV_STATUS channelAllocate(const gpuTsgHandle tsg,
         goto cleanup_free_virtual;
     }
 
+    //
+    // Notification memory has to start out idle (status == 0), but the backing
+    // sysmem is only zeroed when NVreg_InitializeSystemMemoryAllocations is
+    // set; otherwise it may still hold data from a previous user of the pages.
+    // A stale value is indistinguishable from a real channel error, so clear
+    // the whole notifier array (error, work submit token and key rotation)
+    // before it is published to the client.
+    //
+    portMemSet((void *)channel->errorNotifier, 0, errorNotifierSize);
+
     // Let's allocate the channel
     pAllocInfo->gpFifoAllocParams.hObjectError  = hErrorNotifier;
     status = getHandleForVirtualAddr(vaSpace,
@@ -11643,6 +11653,13 @@ NV_STATUS nvGpuOpsPagingChannelAllocate(struct gpuDevice *device,
 
     NV_ASSERT(channel->errorNotifier);
 
+    //
+    // Same as channelAllocate(): the paging channel's notifiers are handed to
+    // the client through channelInfo->shadowErrorNotifier and must not contain
+    // stale data from the previous user of the pages.
+    //
+    portMemSet((void *)channel->errorNotifier, 0, errorNotifierSize);
+
     // Ideally, we need to acquire there locks (in that order):
     // a. RM API lock
     // b. device->handle GPU lock
